  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.0 - Low-precision weights now stay NATIVE in GPU memory instead of being upcast on load: bf16, FP8 (E4M3/E5M2) and quantized int8/uint8 keep their own bytes and are converted per-element in the shader at use. FNUZ FP8 (dtypes 18/20) supported. Causal masks are generated on the GPU rather than uploaded. Browser model loads stream from the OPFS cache without entering the .NET heap. FIXES: bf16/FP8 raw_data was decoded as fp16; ToFloatArray silently returned an ALL-ZERO tensor for any dtype missing from its size map; the OPFS cache stored HTTP error bodies as models; the browser download never actually streamed and retried an OOM by re-allocating. See Changelog.",
